[36m(PPOTrainer pid=1890399)[0m INFO 02-25 14:21:20 ppo_trainer.py:410] [trace] step=45 reward=0.000 response_len=3856 total_len=7435 preview='system name=<|plugin|>\\nYou are an expert reasoner with extensive experience in all areas. You approach problems through systematic thinking and rigorous reasoning. Your response should reflect deep understanding and precise logical thinking, making your solution path and reasoning clear to others. Please put your thinking process within <think>...</think> tags.\\n\\nYour response should consist of a reasoning step (**thought**) followed immediately by a function call in valid JSON format. Wrap each function call using the `<|action_start|><|plugin|>` and `<|action_end|>` tags.\\n\\n**Format example:**\\n\\n```\\n(Your thought goes here...)\\n\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{\\n    "name": "tool_name",\\n    "parameters": {\\n        "parameter1": "value1",\\n        "parameter2": "value2"\\n    }\\n}\\n<|action_end|>\\n```\\n\\n# External Tools\\nYou have access to these tools:\\n[\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_molecular_weight",\\n      "description": "Return the average molecular weight (Daltons).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_exact_molecular_weight",\\n      "description": "Return the monoisotopic exact molecular weight (Daltons).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_heavy_atom_count",\\n      "description": "Return the number of non-hydrogen atoms (heavy atoms).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_mol_logp",\\n      "description": "Return Wildman–Crippen cLogP (octanol/water).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_tpsa",\\n      "description": "Return topological polar surface area TPSA (Å^2).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_hbd",\\n      "description": "Return Lipinski H-bond donors count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_hba",\\n      "description": "Return Lipinski H-bond acceptors count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_rotatable_bonds",\\n      "description": "Return rotatable bonds count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_fraction_csp3",\\n      "description": "Return FractionCSP3 = (# sp3 carbon atoms)/(# total carbon atoms), Often used as a simple “3D character / saturation” proxy from 2D structure.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_mol_mr",\\n      "description": "Return Wildman–Crippen molar refractivity (MR).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_ring_count",\\n      "description": "Return total ring count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_aromatic_rings",\\n      "description": "Return aromatic ring count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_formal_charge",\\n      "description": "Return net formal charge (sum of atom formal charges as encoded in the SMILES).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_qed",\\n      "description": "Return QED (Quantitative Estimate of Drug-likeness) as implemented in RDKit.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_heteroatoms",\\n      "description": "Return heteroatom count (non C/H).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "describe_high_level_fg_fragments",\\n      "description": "Accurately parse functional groups with attachment points, corresponding fragment SMILES, and atom ids in the SMILES string for better structure description.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "The SMILES string to parse."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "remove_salts",\\n      "description": "Desalt a SMILES by removing salts/counterions and keeping ONLY the largest organic fragment. Use this tool when the SMILES contains multiple disconnected components separated by \'.\' and one or more components are likely inorganic ions/solvents (e.g., [Na+], Cl-, Br-, I-, [K+], [Li+], [Ca2+], [Mg2+], [NH4+], sulfate/phosphate, etc.), or when you want the parent (active) molecule for downstream property prediction.\\nIn aqueous/physiological conditions, salts typically dissociate; counterions are usually not part of the parent drug structure for many structure-based predictions.\\nTypical examples needing desalting: \'CC(=O)O.[Na+]\', \'[Na+].O=C(O)c1ccccc1\', \'CCO.Cl\'.\\nDo NOT use if the SMILES is already a single component (no \'.\') or if multiple organic fragments represent real mixture/co-crystal/combination therapy that should be kept. Output is the canonical SMILES of the retained parent fragment; smaller fragments are discarded.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "predict_pka",\\n      "description": "Predict pKa values for ionizable sites in a molecule. Returns base-site and acid-site pKa values (1-indexed atom map numbers), the most basic/acidic pKa, the number of basic/acidic sites, and the atom-mapped SMILES.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "estimate_logd",\\n      "description": "Estimate logD at a target pH from predicted pKa values and RDKit logP. Uses a Henderson-Hasselbalch approximation: logD(pH) ≈ logP + log10(f_neutral). logP is RDKit Wildman-Crippen logP. This is a heuristic intended for helpingyour reasoning and should not be treated as experimental logD. For polyprotic molecules, uses the most basic and most acidic predicted pKa values.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          },\\n          "ph": {\\n            "type": "number",\\n            "description": "Target pH (default: 7.4)."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "score_structural_alerts",\\n      "description": "Screen a molecule against RDKit\'s built-in structural alert catalogs (PAINS, Brenk, NIH, ZINC, ChEMBL, etc.).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          },\\n          "alert_library": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "enum": [\\n              "all",\\n              "pains",\\n              "pains_a",\\n              "pains_b",\\n              "pains_c",\\n              "brenk",\\n              "nih",\\n              "zinc",\\n              "chembl",\\n              "chembl_bms",\\n              "chembl_lint",\\n              "chembl_mlsmr"\\n            ],\\n            "description": "Alert library to screen against (default: all)."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_labute_asa",\\n      "description": "Return Labute approximate surface area (ASA proxy) using RDKit rdMolDescriptors.CalcLabuteASA.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_fraction_aromatic_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return fraction of aromatic atoms (aromatic atoms / total atoms).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_positive_charge_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return count of cationic centers (atoms with formal charge > 0).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_negative_charge_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return count of anionic centers (atoms with formal charge < 0).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n]\\nuser\\nInstructions: Answer the following question about drug properties.\\nContext: When a drug is orally administered, it needs to be absorbed from the human gastrointestinal system into the bloodstream of the human body. This ability of absorption is called human intestinal absorption (HIA) and it is crucial for a drug to be delivered to the target.\\nQuestion: Given a drug SMILES string, predict whether it\\n(A) cannot be absorbed (B) can be absorbed\\nDrug SMILES: O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O\\n\\nPlease think step by step and use tools when necessary (**Don\'t use the same tool more than once**). Then put your final choice ((A) or (B)) after "Answer:"\\nassistant\\n<think>\\nI need to analyze this drug SMILES to predict whether it can be absorbed (HIA) or not. The SMILES is: O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O\\n\\nFirst, I should understand what this molecule is. It looks like a peptide-like structure with multiple chiral centers, a phenyl group, and carboxylic acid groups. Let me parse it: it has two carboxylic acid groups (O=C(O) at the beginning and C(=O)O at the end), an amide bond (N[C@@H]...), and a cyclic structure with a lactam (N2C1=O). This appears to be a dipeptide-like molecule with a phenylalanine side chain (CCc1ccccc1) and a glutamic acid-like group (C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O). Actually, it looks like a cyclic dipeptide (cyclo-dipeptide) with a phenyl group.\\n\\nTo predict HIA, I need to consider properties like molecular weight, logP, hydrogen bond donors/acceptors, polar surface area, etc. Generally, drugs with good oral absorption follow Lipinski\'s Rule of Five: MW < 500, logP < 5, HBD ≤ 5, HBA ≤ 10. Also, TPSA < 140 Å² is often used as a cutoff for good absorption.\\n\\nLet me calculate these properties using the available tools. First, I\'ll get the molecular weight.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_molecular_weight", "parameters": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Average molecular weight (Daltons): 389.4520", "function_name": "get_molecular_weight", "arguments": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nMW is 389.45, which is below 500. Good.\\n\\nNow get logP.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_mol_logp", "parameters": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "cLogP estimate: 1.1170", "function_name": "get_mol_logp", "arguments": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nlogP is 1.12, well below 5. Good.\\n\\nNow HBD and HBA.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_hbd", "parameters": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Number of H-bond donors: 3", "function_name": "get_hbd", "arguments": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nHBD is 3, which is ≤5. Good.\\n\\nNow HBA.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_hba", "parameters": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Number of H-bond acceptors: 5", "function_name": "get_hba", "arguments": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nHBA is 5, which is ≤10. Good.\\n\\nNow TPSA. This is important for absorption. Let\'s get TPSA.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_tpsa", "parameters": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Topological Polar Surface Area (TPSA, \\u00c5^2): 110.1800", "function_name": "get_tpsa", "arguments": {"smiles": "O=C(O)[C@H](CCc1ccccc1)N[C@@H]1CCCN2CCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)N2C1=O"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nTPSA is 110.18 Å². Typically, TPSA < 140 Å² is considered good for absorption. This is below 140.\\n\\nNow, other factors: number of rotatable bonds. Let\'s get that.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_num_