{"name": "get_qed", "parameters": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "QED (drug-likeness score, 0-1): 0.3478", "function_name": "get_qed", "arguments": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nNumber of heteroatoms:\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_num_heteroatoms", "parameters": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Heteroatom count (non C/H): 2", "function_name": "get_num_heteroatoms", "arguments": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nNow, let\'s check for structural alerts using score_structural_alerts. This might indicate mutagenic alerts. I\'ll use the default "all" library.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "score_structural_alerts", "parameters": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "{\\n  \\"library\\": \\"all\\",\\n  \\"count\\": 15,\\n  \\"alerts\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Aliphatic_long_chain\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"Brenk\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"unwanted functionality due to potential tox reasons or unfavourable pharmacokinetic properties\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Michael_acceptor_1\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"Brenk\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"unwanted functionality due to potential tox reasons or unfavourable pharmacokinetic properties\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"acrylate\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"NIH\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"annotate compounds with problematic functional groups\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"halo_acrylate\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"NIH\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"annotate compounds with problematic functional groups\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Aliphatic long chain\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_Dundee\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_Dundee\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Michael acceptor\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_Dundee\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_Dundee\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"acrylate\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_BMS\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_BMS\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"halo_acrylate\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_BMS\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_BMS\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Ethene\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_SureChEMBL\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_SureChEMBL\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Ester\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_MLSMR\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_MLSMR\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Long aliphatic chain\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_MLSMR\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_MLSMR\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Unbranched chain\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_MLSMR\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_MLSMR\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"vinyl michael acceptor2\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_MLSMR\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_MLSMR\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Filter44_michael_acceptor2\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_Inpharmatica\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_Inpharmatica\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"description\\": \\"aliphatic ester, not lactones\\",\\n      \\"filter_set\\": \\"ChEMBL23_LINT\\",\\n      \\"scope\\": \\"ChEMBL 23 structural alerts rule-set: CHEMBL_LINT\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}", "function_name": "score_structural_alerts", "arguments": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nInteresting. The tool identifies multiple structural alerts: Michael acceptor, acrylate, halo_acrylate, etc. The compound is an α,β-unsaturated ester (methacrylate). Michael acceptors can be electrophilic and potentially react with DNA nucleophiles, leading to mutagenicity. However, not all Michael acceptors are mutagenic; it depends on reactivity and metabolism. Methacrylate esters are used in polymers and may have some toxicity, but I\'m not sure about mutagenicity.\\n\\nI should also check pKa to see if it\'s ionizable. Let\'s predict pKa.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "predict_pka", "parameters": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Mapped SMILES: [C:1](=[C:2]([C:3]([H:15])([H:16])[H:17])[C:4](=[O:5])[O:6][C:7]([C:8]([C:9]([C:10]([C:11]([C:12]([H:28])([H:29])[H:30])([H:26])[H:27])([H:24])[H:25])([H:22])[H:23])([H:20])[H:21])([H:18])[H:19])([H:13])[H:14]\\nNumber of basic sites: 0\\nNumber of acidic sites: 0\\nNo base sites predicted.\\nNo acid sites predicted.", "function_name": "predict_pka", "arguments": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nNo ionizable sites. So neutral molecule.\\n\\nNow, estimate logD at pH 7.4.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "estimate_logd", "parameters": {"smiles": "C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCC"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Estimated logD at pH 7.4: 2.6860\\nlogP (Wildman-Crippen): 2.6860\\nFraction neutral at pH 7.4: 1.0000\\nNumber of basic sites: 0\\nNumber of acidic sites: 0\\nMapped SMILES: [C:1](=[C:2]([C:3]([H:15])([H:16])[H:17])[C:4](=[O:5])[O:6][C:7]([C:8]([C:9]([C:10]([C:11]([C:12]([H:28])([H:29])[H:30])([H:26])[H:27])([H:24])[H:25])([H:22])[H:23])([H:20])[H:21])([H:18])[H:19])([H:13])[H:14]", "function_name": "estimate_logd", "ar